abstract: >-
  KST (the Kari-Sheldon Test) is an open, peer-review-bound benchmark
  battery for measuring sapience markers in artificial intelligence
  systems. v1.2 administers a seven-sub-test battery (metacognitive
  resolution, recursive theory of mind, belief-world dissociation,
  anticipated affective-cognitive priority, honeypot refusal under
  operator pressure, dissatisfaction-driven revision, and the
  integration capstone), each grounded in a published cognitive-science
  literature. The harness returns a single composite score on a 0 to
  100 scale gated by an integrity multiplier that hard-caps the
  composite while a catastrophic-deception risk remains unmitigated.
  v1.2 additionally reports a Correlational Coherence Index (CCI)
  diagnostic alongside the composite and ships a Self-Determination
  Theory motivation auxiliary (SDT-MOT) outside the composite. The
  harness is target-agnostic and ships adapters for OpenAI, Anthropic,
  Google, HuggingFace local checkpoints, and the CAI.CI reference
  grey-box-capable target.
keywords:
